  subgraph LAW["⚖️ THE LAW — 20 CLAUSES. EVERY ONE WAS PAID FOR."]
    Z1["1. **node --check PROVES NOTHING.** It passed on a ZERO-BYTE spice.js.<br/><br/>2. **A REPORT IS NOT PROOF. A PASSING TEST IS A REPORT TOO.**<br/>PROVE IT PER-SECTION. **A BAD ROOM HIDES INSIDE A GOOD AGGREGATE.**<br/>🩸 12 Jul: THIS LAW CAUGHT ITS OWN AUTHOR. Code shipped a written proof-by-trace for<br/>the back button. The trace was CORRECT. The fix is LIVE. **THE BUG IS STILL THERE.**<br/><br/>3. **SILENT WRONG IS WORSE THAN LOUD MISSING.**<br/><br/>4. A NARROW QUESTION GETS A NARROW ANSWER — AND IT WILL BE TRUE.<br/>**ASK 'WHAT IS NOT GUARDED?' — NEVER 'is X guarded?'**<br/><br/>5. LOCALHOST IS NOT LIVE. COMMITTED IS NOT PUSHED. PUSHED IS NOT DEPLOYED.<br/>**AND DEPLOYED IS NOT PUBLISHED.** (Netlify built 508cd4c and kept serving the old one.)<br/><br/>6. **DON'T PATCH N SITES. BUILD THE ONE THING THEY SHOULD ALL CALL.**<br/><br/>7. A BLANK IS A BUG. A TEASER IS A PITCH. THE LOCK IS THE SALESMAN.<br/><br/>8. 'SHIP IT' IS NOT 'PUSH IT'. SAY WHICH ONE YOU MEAN.<br/><br/>9. **A CONTEXT-DEPENDENT RULE MUST NEVER BE ENCODED AS A CONTEXT-FREE ALIAS.**<br/>The Meat Cut Guide is a METHOD→CUT rule. An alias does not know the method.<br/>Flatten one into the other and **A GOOD RULE BECOMES A SILENT LIE.** (lamb → lamb neck.)<br/><br/>10. **THE BUG WAS IN THE DATA, NOT THE CODE.** The resolver was never lying.<br/>**IT WAS FAITHFULLY READING LIES WE WROTE OURSELVES.** Guards are the NET. Data is the FIX.<br/><br/>11. **NO MODEL AUTHORS A PRICE** … and 🆕 **LAW 11 DOES NOT CARE WHO WROTE THE NUMBER<br/>DOWN.** It was aimed at Code. Then lamb mince came in at R98 — 2.2x under, and almost<br/>certainly **BEEF MINCE WEARING A LAMB LABEL. TINA'S OWN NOTE.**<br/>**A NUMBER THAT SITS IN THE NOTES LONG ENOUGH STARTS TO LOOK LIKE A FACT.**<br/>src + when + conf, or it doesn't ship. conf:'online' is not conf:'shelf'.<br/><br/>12. FAIL-LOUD IS THE NET. **PRICED-CORRECTLY IS THE GOAL.**<br/>Don't ship 7 loud blanks when the answer was already sitting in the database.<br/><br/>13. **A GUARD THAT NULLS A CORRECT ANSWER IS A BUG, NOT A SAFETY FEATURE.**<br/>L3 nulled 'coconut oil for frying'. A correct key. **L3 DIED ON ITS OWN EVIDENCE.**<br/><br/>14. **DRY-RUN BEFORE SHIP.** Code proposed L3, dry-ran it, and KILLED ITS OWN DESIGN.<br/>**EVERY GUARD GETS ITS FALSE-POSITIVE LIST BEFORE IT IS BUILT.**<br/><br/>15. **A RULING THAT LIVES ONLY IN THE CHAT IS NOT A RULING.** IT GOES IN THE BRIEF.<br/><br/>16. **A COOK'S RULE IS NOT A SHOPPER'S RULE.** 'Stewing lamb = shoulder or neck' is<br/>TRUE IN THE KITCHEN AND USELESS AT THE TILL. **YOU CANNOT BUY 'SHOULDER OR NECK'.**<br/>👉 **IF A KEY IS NOT SOMETHING A HUMAN CAN PUT IN A TROLLEY, IT IS NOT A KEY.**<br/><br/>17. **CONTEXT-FLATTENING HAPPENS AT THE KEY LEVEL TOO**, not just the alias level.<br/>'lamb knuckle / potjiekos' merges a CUT with a MIX. 'lamb stew / lamb mince' merges<br/>GROUND with CUBED BONE-IN. **A MERGED KEY AVERAGES A REAL DIFFERENCE INTO A FAKE ONE.**<br/><br/>18. **RECONCILE, DO NOT ADD.** A new key beside an old key for the SAME PRODUCT gives<br/>you TWO PRICES AND A COIN TOSS. Print the current list. Sign one number. THEN write.<br/><br/>19. 🆕 **A METRIC THAT DOESN'T EXIST IS A BUG YOU CANNOT SEE.** 53 WK cards were<br/>priceless this morning and NOBODY HAD EVER COUNTED THEM. We proved ingredient LINES<br/>all day and never counted CARDS — **the only thing the user actually sees.**<br/><br/>20. 🆕 **A CARD THAT PRICES SOME OF THE FOOD IS WORSE THAN A CARD THAT PRICES NONE.**<br/>A blank invites a question. **A PARTIAL TOTAL ANSWERS ONE THAT WAS NEVER ASKED,<br/>WRONGLY, WITH A NUMBER THE USER WILL ACT ON.**<br/>(Lamb Tagine · R38 · and there is no lamb in it.)"]
  end

  subgraph LATENT["⏳ LATENT · LAUNCH · CONTENT"]
